## Weight distributions

With only 1,000 people representing 7.2 million, the average projected weight is roughly 7,200 — each panelist "stands in" for about 7,200 individuals. The full TAM panel carries much smaller weights (mean ≈ 2,000) because it has far more members spread across the same universe, so each person represents fewer individuals.


