The raincloud adds the raw points (a 300-member sample per group) beneath each half-violin, making the actual data density visible alongside the smoothed shape and the box.

## Matching the spot list

The spot list contains GRPs already computed for the **Arab 15+ / million-plus cities** target group and covers the same week.

For every spot we compute:

> **GRPAbsolute** = sum of projected weights of all sample members watching the spot's **channel** in the **minute the spot starts**, on the spot's **date** — using that day's weights.

The same calculation, applied to the filtered TAM panel with its official weights (`INDWgt`), reproduces the benchmark and validates the method.


::: {.cell}

:::


Of the **1097 spots** in the list, **942** have a recalculated GRP matching the spots file and are kept for the comparison. The 10 samples found viewers for **546** of these — the remainder aired in minutes where no sampled panelist was watching that channel.

