## Takeaways

- **Target group:** Arabs aged 15+ in five million-plus cities — a universe of 7.2 million, roughly 42% of the full TAM universe
- A 1,000-person sample carries **high projected weights** (\~7,200 per person), so single-spot GRPs are driven by very few viewers
- Spot-level estimates are therefore **volatile** — the CV column flags spots where the 10 samples disagree strongly
- Aggregated (campaign-level) GRPs are far more stable than individual spot GRPs
- Overnight spots carry high GRPs that the small samples capture less well
